@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity] fleet-monitor-independent-budget
Detailed collection MUST NOT call compute admission or mutate Lilly execution
state. Inputs, entity counts, subprocess duration and retry storage MUST be
bounded. Collection/export failure MUST NOT stop guests or authorize capacity.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product] fleet-monitor-measurement-identity
Counter rates MUST require matching host boot and entity incarnation, increasing
monotonic time and nondecreasing counters. Missing/reset/stale observations MUST
remain unknown; zero MUST remain a valid observation. Fleet totals MUST separate
physical capacity from logical allocations and nested workload consumption.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] fleet-monitor-safe-host-projection
Only allowlisted numeric resource and aggregate proxy metrics, bounded infrastructure identities and
the updater's validated intended/observed revision, phase and failure labels and
allowlisted backup states, timestamps, durations and counts may
leave the host. Guest
processes, command lines, environments, raw machine ID, credential contents and
arbitrary unit properties MUST NOT enter samples or logs.
